      "message": "Hmm, I didn\u0027t consider the interrupt trigger type.  The Nuvoton MIWU (Multi-Input Wake-Up) module supports level or edge events, plus rising/falling/both.  So we really need a device tree property to set the trigger type.\n\nA recent change just merged adding [GPIO hog](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/54110) support.  That change provides a mechanism to configure GPIOs during system initialization.  This is similar to what we do with the `named-gpios` node now.\n\nLet me take a stab at a migration plan to adding in GPIO hog support before  we try to get the Intel board updated to use the shared TCPC interrupt handler.",
